module test.claim.compute.output_capture_absence_wet_witness

// WET EXECUTING-ROUTE WITNESS FOR THE BUILD-OUTPUT CAPTURE (Charter 2; manager ruling of
// 2026-10-19: the inhabittance rows must EXECUTE production's route -- "a grep is not a consumer",
// DESIGN 5).
//
// WHAT THIS FILE ADDS OVER THE HERMETIC ONE.
// test.claim.compute.output_capture_absence_witness supplies readings as data and pins the route
// with the compiler-reflected call walk. That shows production's route CAN reach the capture step;
// it cannot show the route RAN, nor that the refusal it returns carries what the real git printed.
// This file EXECUTES production's own
//   compute_return_outputs(instance, layout, declared)
// -- no wrapper, no re-fold, no supplied pair, no new transport mock arm -- against a real
// temporary checkout and the real /usr/bin/git, on the runner's own host. The effects are the ones
// the self-host runs: compute_exec -> gunbc.WitnessBin.Run for `git hash-object` and for the
// staging install. Wet is what `gunbc run --claim-run` gets without --dry-run: `run_verb` in
// src/v1/stage0/src/main.rs selects ExecutionMode::Hermetic when --dry-run is given and
// ExecutionMode::Wet when it is not, and the comment beside that choice reads "--dry-run means
// Hermetic, which REFUSES host operations rather than mocking them silently, and absence means
// Wet". No mock arm is added to the transport to make these rows hermetic:
// gunbc.hermetic_mock_fidelity `fabricated_fact_next_trigger` requires an arm to answer as a
// function of the operation's declared inputs, `eval_mock_response` binds no inputs today, and the
// unconditional alternative is the arm class that module filed as a defect and had deleted on
// 2026-08-23 (`mock_arm_is_fabricating`, `hermetic_mock_fidelity_rows`).
//
// establishes them: production's own route, run against a real git.
//  (1) PRESENT. One declared output exists on disk. The route must return it with a blob that
//      EQUALS git hash-object's OWN stdout. Nothing is typed from memory: the expectation is
//      captured in the same run by the same /usr/bin/git twice over -- `hash-object <path>` in the
//      same workdir on the same absolute path, and `hash-object --no-filters --stdin` over the same
//      bytes -- and all three live readings plus capture_bytes_oid must agree with the blob
//      production returned.
//  (2) ABSENT. One declared output was never written. The route must refuse, and the detail must
//      carry git's REAL exit code and stderr AS CAPTURED IN THIS RUN: the expected exit and stderr
//      come from running that same `git hash-object <that absolute path>` in that same workdir
//      through the independent compute_exec route, outside the capture step. If git changes its
//      exit or its message, this row follows git rather than a string I wrote.
//
// CONTAINMENT -- a claim every row must return, not a promise in a comment (review 82796: an
// earlier revision compared the WHOLE /tmp listing before and after, which made an unrelated
// process's /tmp traffic able to fail the run).
// Everything this file creates lives under ONE shell.Mktemp.DirWithTemplate root, reached through the
// INSTANCE's own roots, so what stays contained is production's path derivation rather than mine:
// instance_root (hence compute_root, hence layout.checkout / work_dir / target_dir) and the
// materialization store are both under the root, and the store is WitnessScratchRoot, so
// layout.staging_dir is <root>/store-staging instead of the fleet's frame scratch.
// The guard therefore says three things, and none of them is a host-wide directory diff (an earlier
// revision compared the whole /tmp listing before and after; review 82796 rightly refused it, because
// another session's /tmp traffic could then fail this row):
//   * production_paths_stay_inside_root -- every path compute_layout derives (checkout, work_dir,
//     target_dir, and the capture's staging_dir) sits under THIS case's temp root, and the staging
//     tree does not sit under materialization_store_frame_root_prefix, which is the fleet's frame
//     scratch at /tmp/gunbc_compute_*. Production owns that derivation, and the root is reached only
//     through the instance's own roots, so this IS the statement that every write stays inside.
//   * root_lists_own_writes -- a recursive find under the root NAMES the file this case wrote. The
//     positive half, so containment cannot pass by listing nothing.
//   * the tree is removed and the host then answers not_found for the root.
// WRITE ROOTS, ENUMERATED (every write a case performs, none outside the Mktemp root R):
//   R itself (shell.Mktemp.DirWithTemplate) and its removal; R/checkout (repo_root bootstrap);
//   the layout trees R/compute/work/<id>/{src,target,out/captured} (compute_ensure_dir and the
//   Filesystem.Write of the declared output); R/store-staging (compute_ensure_dir, then the
//   capture's `install -m 0755`). `git hash-object` is run without -w and HashObjectStdinNoWrite
//   writes nothing. The frame scratch /tmp/gunbc_compute_<frame> enters only through a
//   FrameJobWorkspace store root, which this fixture never supplies: the instance's roots
//   (instance_root, store root) are the only inputs production derives its paths from, and both
//   are children of R. Its sorted population is still listed BEFORE and AFTER and carried in the
//   case record as REPORTED evidence, not as a verdict input. A refused listing is named as a
//   refusal, never read as empty.
//
// ENROLLMENT, all three rows (the incomplete triple is the failure chunk_21's header documents):
//   1. v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal local_repo_wet_schedule -- one WetScheduledClaim per
//      identity below. This is the ROUTE; without it nothing executes these rows.
//   2. gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier -- pattern
//      "output_capture_absence_wet_witness.dag", classification LocalRepoWetLane, so hermetic
//      discovery does not claim a file whose effects it cannot serve.
//   3. v2.workflow.floor_route_gap (floor_route_gap_expectation_chunk_45) -- one expectation per
//      identity, operation DirWithTemplate, ground NoMockResponse: what the hermetic route refuses
//      on, read from THESE identities by the hermetic claim run itself
//      (`gunbc run --claim-run --dry-run --function <row>` reports HostEffectRefused {
//      operation: "DirWithTemplate", ground: NoMockResponse }), which is the operation the case root
//      is created through. Not copied from a sibling: copying is what chunk_21's header records as
//      producing floor_route_gap_expectation_mismatch.

import std.types { Bool, Int, NonEmptyStr, String }
import std.algebra { string_contains, trim }
import std.optional { Present, Absent }
import extdeps.shell
import extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io { Filesystem }
import extdeps.git
import extdeps.git.plumbing
import gunbc.compute.work_request { DeclaredOutput, CheckoutRoot }
import gunbc.compute.compute_attempt_slots_root { compute_seat_path, ComputeFlatSeat }
import gunbc.compute.work_provider_local {
  ComputeExec,
  ComputeExecFailed,
  ComputeExecOk,
  ComputeLayout,
  OutputsMismatch,
  OutputsReturned,
  compute_exec,
  compute_ensure_dir,
  compute_layout,
  compute_program,
  compute_return_outputs,
  compute_staged_path,
}
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_execution_contract {
  AttemptStateDirectoryCapability,
  GitWorkspaceCapability,
}
import gunbc.managed_directory { declared_directory_mode, DirectoryOwnerAllEveryoneTraverse }
import extdeps.tools.gnu_coreutils { coreutils_install_directories_arguments }
import gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance {
  HostDashboardInstance,
  IsolatedJobToolchainHomes,
  DashboardExistingProviderState,
  DashboardExistingRepo,
  DashboardLocalProvision,
  DashboardObserveOnly,
  DashboardToolchain,
  DispatchStateInstanceOwned,
  WorkerIsServiceUser,
  admitted_single_session_binding,
  codex_roadmap_account_evidence,
  dashboard_execution_environment_for_toolchain,
  dashboard_instance_child,
  dashboard_named_tmux_server,
  dispatch_worker_memory_ceiling,
  fleet_admitted_revision_source,
  fleet_compute_hermetic_dashboard_id,
  fleet_compute_hermetic_deployment,
  fleet_compute_hermetic_directory_owner,
  fleet_compute_hermetic_toolchain,
}
import std.materialization_store_grant {
  MaterializationStoreRoot,
  WitnessScratchRoot,
  materialization_store_frame_root_prefix,
}

// THE ONE FACT THIS FILE TYPES: the bytes of the present declared output. Used three times --
// written into the checkout, hashed independently by git to name the expected blob, and hashed by
// production's own route.
data capture_bytes: String = "gunbc capture wet witness fixed bytes 0123456789\n"

// WHAT GIT ITSELF PRINTS FOR THOSE BYTES (measured on the runner: `git hash-object --no-filters
// --stdin` over capture_bytes). Pinned so a silent change in WHAT the capture hashes -- hashing the
// staged file instead of the source, or a different filter -- surfaces as a disagreement between
// live readings, not as a number I could rewrite to match the bug.
data capture_bytes_oid: String = "cc815613cfd8c8f3870be038765d840d7c656d02"

// The declared output paths, relative to the checkout root.
data capture_rel: String = "out/captured/plan.json"
data capture_rel_absent: String = "out/captured/absent.json"

// The basename the recursive listing under the root looks for, so containment is proved by a
// recursive find over absolute paths rather than by a single directory's bare-name listing.
data capture_file_name: String = "plan.json"

// THE TEMP ROOT'S OWN NAME. mktemp's plain Dir yields /tmp/tmp.XXXXXX, which fails
// is_gunbc_tmp_scratch_store_root ("/tmp/gunbc_*"), and a WitnessScratchRoot outside that namespace
// admits NOTHING (materialization_store_envelope returns an empty envelope) -- so the capture's own
// staging write would be refused for a naming reason rather than a behaviour one. The template puts
// the root in the scratch namespace while staying clear of the fleet's /tmp/gunbc_compute_ prefix.
data witness_root_template: String = "/tmp/gunbc_capture_wet_XXXXXX"

// THE WITNESS'S OWN HOST: the production constructor shape (cf.
// fleet_compute_hermetic_dashboard_instance_at) with exactly three departures, all toward
// containment -- repo_root/origin are the temp checkout, and BOTH roots production derives capture
// paths from (instance_root, and the materialization store, which is WitnessScratchRoot here) sit
// under one temp root.
fn witness_instance(temp_root: String) -> HostDashboardInstance {
  let homes = IsolatedJobToolchainHomes {
    cargo_home: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "homes/cargo"),
    rustup_home: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "homes/rustup"),
  }
  let toolchain: DashboardToolchain = fleet_compute_hermetic_toolchain(homes: homes)
  HostDashboardInstance {
    deployment: fleet_compute_hermetic_deployment,
    instance_id: fleet_compute_hermetic_dashboard_id,
    host_identity: "wet-capture-witness" as NonEmptyStr,
    provision_parent_root: temp_root as FilePath,
    instance_root: temp_root as FilePath,
    local_origin_root: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "origin"),
    local_origin_publish_ref: "refs/heads/main" as NonEmptyStr,
    repo_root: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "checkout"),
    dispatch_base_ref: "origin/main" as NonEmptyStr,
    publication_base_branch: "main" as NonEmptyStr,
    dispatch_state_scope: DispatchStateInstanceOwned {
      worktree_child: "attempts" as NonEmptyStr,
      attempt_state_child: "attempt-state" as NonEmptyStr,
    },
    execution_environment: dashboard_execution_environment_for_toolchain(
      toolchain: toolchain,
      serve_binary: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "bin/gunbc"),
    ),
    provider_state: DashboardExistingProviderState {
      root: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "codex"),
      executable: none,
      binding: admitted_single_session_binding(
        selection: CodexDefaultAccount,
        evidence: codex_roadmap_account_evidence,
      ),
    },
    serve_binary: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "bin/gunbc"),
    serve_function: "roadmap_serve_handle" as NonEmptyStr,
    listen_host: "127.0.0.1" as NonEmptyStr,
    listen_port: 18099,
    tmux_server: dashboard_named_tmux_server(instance_id: fleet_compute_hermetic_dashboard_id),
    actuation: DashboardObserveOnly,
    provision_transport: DashboardLocalProvision,
    source_seed: DashboardExistingRepo { anchor_ref: "origin/main" as NonEmptyStr },
    admitted_revision: fleet_admitted_revision_source,
    toolchain: toolchain,
    dispatch_worker_memory_max: dispatch_worker_memory_ceiling,
    directory_owner: fleet_compute_hermetic_directory_owner,
    worker: WorkerIsServiceUser,
    materialization_store_root: Present {
      value: WitnessScratchRoot {
        root: dashboard_instance_child(root: temp_root as FilePath, child: "store") as String,
      },
    },
  }
}

// THE FLEET'S OWN FRAME SCRATCH, listed BEFORE AND AFTER and carried in the case record (the
// manager's ruling asks for that listing). It is EVIDENCE, not a verdict input: whether an unrelated
// process touched /tmp cannot decide whether THIS run stayed inside its temp dir -- that is decided
// by production_paths_stay_inside_root, which speaks directly about the paths production derived.
// A refusal to list is NAMED as a refusal, never read as an empty population.
fn fleet_scratch_listing() -> String {
  let listed = shell.Find.FilesByNameSorted(
    root: "/tmp" as FilePath,
    name_glob: join([materialization_store_frame_root_prefix, "*"], "") as NonEmptyStr,
  )
  let ok = listed.success
  let listed_body = trim(s: listed.stdout)
  let refused = join(["<frame-scratch listing refused: ", trim(s: listed.stderr), ">"], "")
  if ok { listed_body } else { refused }
}

// THE CONTAINMENT CLAIM ITSELF. compute_layout derives checkout/work_dir/target_dir/staging_dir from
// the instance, so asserting each sits under this case's mktemp root IS the statement "every write
// this route performs stays inside the temp dir" -- said about production's own derived paths rather
// than inferred from a directory diff. The second half is the departure WitnessScratchRoot buys: the
// staging tree the capture installs into must NOT be the fleet's frame scratch, so it may not sit
// under the frame-scratch prefix even though both live under /tmp.
fn production_paths_stay_inside_root(layout: ComputeLayout, instance: HostDashboardInstance, root: String) -> Bool {
  let under = join([root, "/"], "")
  layout.root.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.work_dir.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.checkout.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.out_dir.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.leases_dir.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.lease_path.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.staging_dir.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.target_dir.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.log_path.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && layout.consumption_path.starts_with(prefix: under)
    && (compute_seat_path(instance: instance, seat: ComputeFlatSeat) as String).starts_with(prefix: under)
    && !layout.staging_dir.starts_with(prefix: materialization_store_frame_root_prefix)
}

// EVERY PATH UNDER THE ROOT, recursively, as absolute paths -- shell.Find.Files runs
// `find <root> -name <glob>`, so its stdout carries full paths, which Filesystem.List's bare
// directory names could not. A refusal is NAMED as a refusal rather than read as an empty tree.
fn root_listing(root: String) -> String {
  let found = shell.Find.FilesByNameSorted(root: root as FilePath, name_glob: capture_file_name as NonEmptyStr)
  let ok = found.success
  let listed_body = found.stdout
  let refused = join(["<root listing refused:", trim(s: found.stderr), ">"], "")
  if ok { listed_body } else { refused }
}

fn root_is_gone(root: String) -> Bool {
  let gone = Filesystem.List(path: root)
  !gone.success && gone.error_kind == "not_found"
}

// WHAT ONE WET CASE PRODUCES. Every field is a live reading or a live effect check, so a row's
// verdict cannot be satisfied by anything I prepared.
type WetCaptureCase {
  // production's verdict rendered: "<declared>=<blob>" for a return, the detail text for a refusal.
  verdict_text: String
  // Present case: the staged file exists in the layout's staging tree (the install ran).
  // Refusing cases: that tree is empty (no install ran at all).
  staging_as_expected: Bool
  // production's own derived layout paths all sit under the case root, staging is NOT under the
  // fleet's frame-scratch prefix, the tree was removed, and the host answers not_found for it.
  contained: Bool
  // The fleet's frame-scratch listing before and after the run -- reported evidence, so the body can
  // show the scratch was never entered; not a verdict input (see fleet_scratch_listing).
  scratch_before: String
  scratch_after: String
  // The root listing named the file this case wrote -- the positive half of containment, kept
  // separate so a vacuously empty listing cannot pass.
  root_lists_own_writes: Bool
  // git's OWN exit code as a string for `hash-object <the absent absolute path>` in the same
  // workdir, taken outside the capture step. "<ok>" when git unexpectedly succeeds.
  truth_exit: String
  // git's OWN stderr for that same command; "" when git unexpectedly succeeds.
  truth_stderr: String
  // git's OWN oid for the present bytes, read two ways: `hash-object <path>` in the same workdir,
  // and `hash-object --no-filters --stdin` over the bytes.
  live_path_oid: String
  live_stdin_oid: String
  // Why a non-verdict happened, when it did -- so a row fails on a named cause, never silently.
  setup_failure: String
}

fn setup_failed(cause: String) -> WetCaptureCase {
  WetCaptureCase {
    verdict_text: "setup failed",
    staging_as_expected: false,
    contained: false,
    scratch_before: "",
    scratch_after: "",
    root_lists_own_writes: false,
    truth_exit: "",
    truth_stderr: "",
    live_path_oid: "",
    live_stdin_oid: "",
    setup_failure: cause,
  }
}


// THE CASE, EXECUTED. write_output=true puts the declared output on disk inside the production
// checkout path; false leaves it unwritten. second_output_present adds a SECOND, present declared
// output AFTER the absent one, so only a stop at the first refusal can keep its install from
// running.
// THE ONE BOOTSTRAP CALL, and it exists for exactly one reason that is a fact about production's
// helper rather than a convenience: compute_ensure_dir launches `install -d` with `workdir` set to
// the instance's REPO ROOT, so it cannot create the repo root itself -- measured on the runner, the
// call succeeds with an existing workdir and fails with repo_root before anything has made it. In
// the fleet, the repo root is created by the provisioner before any compute work runs; a wet case
// that builds its own host has to make that one directory. Everything BELOW it -- the layout's
// checkout, target and staging trees -- then goes through production's own compute_ensure_dir,
// unchanged. Same program, same capability lookup, same mode, same argument builder as that helper;
// only the launched-from directory differs, and only for this call. A refusal returns false.
fn compute_ensure_dir_from(instance: HostDashboardInstance, root: String, path: String) -> Bool {
  let install = compute_program(instance: instance, cap: AttemptStateDirectoryCapability)
  let dir_mode = declared_directory_mode(m: DirectoryOwnerAllEveryoneTraverse)
  match compute_exec(
    program: install,
    workdir: root,
    args: coreutils_install_directories_arguments(mode: dir_mode, paths: [path]),
  ) {
    ComputeExecOk { stdout: _, stderr: _ } => true
    ComputeExecFailed { exit_code: _, stdout: _, stderr: _ } => false
  }
}

fn wet_capture_case(write_output: Bool, second_output_present: Bool) -> WetCaptureCase {
  let root = shell.Mktemp.DirWithTemplate(template: witness_root_template).path as String
  let instance = witness_instance(temp_root: root)
  let scratch_before = fleet_scratch_listing()
  let layout_opt = compute_layout(instance: instance, identity_hex: "wetcapturewitnessidentity0000000000")
  let checkout = match layout_opt {
    Absent => join([root, "/no-layout"], "")
    Present { value: layout } => layout.checkout
  }
  let dirs_ready = match layout_opt {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: layout } =>
      compute_ensure_dir_from(instance: instance, root: root, path: instance.repo_root as String)
        && compute_ensure_dir(instance: instance, path: layout.checkout)
        && compute_ensure_dir(instance: instance, path: layout.target_dir)
        && compute_ensure_dir(instance: instance, path: layout.staging_dir)
        && compute_ensure_dir(instance: instance, path: join([layout.checkout, "/out/captured"], ""))
  }
  // THE LAYOUT'S OWN DIRECTORIES, created by production's own helper over the same paths
  // compute_spawn_and_collect creates (checkout, target_dir, staging_dir), after ONE bootstrap call
  // that only makes the instance's repo root -- which the fleet's provisioner creates before any
  // compute work, and which compute_ensure_dir cannot make for itself because it launches `install
  // -d` from there (see compute_ensure_dir_from; both facts were measured on the runner, not
  // assumed). Every result is checked and a refusal names itself below. Nothing here fabricates a
  // directory the route would not have made: the helper, the capability, the mode and the argument
  // builder are production's.
  //
  // The last path above is the directory a BUILD makes for its own artifact: the route never
  // creates an output's directory (compute_spawn_and_collect ensures the layout's own trees, the
  // build writes its declared outputs, and the capture only READS them afterwards), so a built
  // work-unit has that parent directory and the layout helpers do not create it. It is made here by
  // production's own compute_ensure_dir, which works unmodified now that repo_root exists.
  //
  // One named failure, not a silent false. The checkout DIRECTORY exists by here (dirs_ready came
  // from compute_ensure_dir over the layout's own paths), so when a declared output is absent,
  // git's refusal is about the missing FILE -- which is what the absent claim is about -- and not
  // an artifact of a missing directory.
  if !dirs_ready {
    setup_failed(cause: "install -d refused for the layout's own paths")
  } else {
    let present_path = join([checkout, "/", capture_rel], "")
    let absent_path = join([checkout, "/", capture_rel_absent], "")
    let written = Filesystem.Write(path: present_path, content: capture_bytes).success
    // THE INDEPENDENT READINGS, from the same /usr/bin/git the instance's capability table names, on
    // the SAME absolute paths in the SAME workdir -- taken outside the capture step, so what each
    // row compares against is git's own output in this run.
    let git_program = compute_program(instance: instance, cap: GitWorkspaceCapability)
    let truth = compute_exec(program: git_program, workdir: checkout, args: ["hash-object", absent_path])
    let path_reading = compute_exec(program: git_program, workdir: checkout, args: ["hash-object", present_path])
    let stdin_reading = git.Plumbing.HashObjectStdinNoWrite(content: capture_bytes)
    let truth_exit = match truth {
      ComputeExecFailed { exit_code, stdout: _, stderr: _ } => to_string(exit_code)
      ComputeExecOk { stdout: _, stderr: _ } => "<ok>"
    }
    let truth_stderr = match truth {
      ComputeExecFailed { exit_code: _, stdout: _, stderr } => trim(s: stderr)
      ComputeExecOk { stdout: _, stderr: _ } => ""
    }
    let live_path_oid = match path_reading {
      ComputeExecFailed { exit_code: _, stdout: _, stderr: _ } => "<path hash refused>"
      ComputeExecOk { stdout, stderr: _ } => trim(s: stdout)
    }
    let live_stdin_oid = trim(s: stdin_reading.oid)
    let declared =
      if write_output {
        [DeclaredOutput { root: CheckoutRoot, path: capture_rel }]
      } else {
        // ORDER IS THE POINT: the absent one first, the present one second.
        [
          DeclaredOutput { root: CheckoutRoot, path: capture_rel_absent },
          DeclaredOutput { root: CheckoutRoot, path: capture_rel },
        ]
      }
    // >>> THE ROUTE ITSELF, production's, executed wet.
    let verdict = match layout_opt {
      Absent => OutputsMismatch { detail: "layout refused" }
      Present { value: layout } =>
        compute_return_outputs(instance: instance, layout: layout, declared: declared)
    }
    // The staging tree: the present case expects the staged file (the install ran); the refusing
    // case expects it EMPTY, including for the second output, which really is on disk.
    let staging_as_expected = match layout_opt {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: layout } =>
        if write_output {
          Filesystem.Read(path: compute_staged_path(layout: layout, declared: capture_rel)).success
        } else {
          let listed = Filesystem.List(path: layout.staging_dir)
          listed.success && trim(s: listed.entries) == ""
        }
    }
    let tree = root_listing(root: root)
    // The positive half: the recursive listing under the root sees the file this case wrote, at a
    // path under the root. Without it, containment could be satisfied by a blind or empty listing.
    let root_lists_own_writes =
      !string_contains(s: tree, pattern: "<root listing refused")
        && string_contains(s: tree, pattern: root)
        && string_contains(s: tree, pattern: capture_file_name)
    let scratch_after = fleet_scratch_listing()
    let removed = shell.Remove.RecursiveForce(path: root as FilePath).success
    let paths_contained = match layout_opt {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: layout } => production_paths_stay_inside_root(layout: layout, instance: instance, root: root)
    }
    let contained = paths_contained && removed && root_is_gone(root: root)
    let verdict_text = match verdict {
      OutputsMismatch { detail: d } => d
      OutputsReturned { outputs: outs } =>
        match outs |> first {
          Present { value: o } => join([o.declared, "=", o.blob], "|")
          Absent => "<empty return>"
        }
    }
    if !written {
      setup_failed(cause: "the declared output could not be written into the checkout")
    } else {
      WetCaptureCase {
        verdict_text: verdict_text,
        staging_as_expected: staging_as_expected,
        contained: contained,
        root_lists_own_writes: root_lists_own_writes,
        scratch_before: scratch_before,
        scratch_after: scratch_after,
        truth_exit: truth_exit,
        truth_stderr: truth_stderr,
        live_path_oid: live_path_oid,
        live_stdin_oid: live_stdin_oid,
        setup_failure: "",
      }
    }
  }
}


// (1) THE PRESENT CLAIM, EXECUTED WET. Production's own route returns the declared output and its
// blob equals git hash-object's OWN stdout -- four live readings of the same bytes agreeing: the
// route's blob, `hash-object <path>` in the same workdir, `hash-object --stdin` over the bytes, and
// the byte-pinned oid. The staged file exists, so the install really ran. Containment is part of
// what the row returns.
test fn the_wet_route_returns_the_blob_git_hash_object_itself_printed() -> Bool {
  let c = wet_capture_case(write_output: true, second_output_present: false)
  c.setup_failure == ""
    && c.contained
    && c.root_lists_own_writes
    && c.staging_as_expected
    && c.live_stdin_oid == capture_bytes_oid
    && c.live_path_oid == capture_bytes_oid
    && c.verdict_text == join([capture_rel, "=", capture_bytes_oid], "|")
}

// (2) THE ABSENT CLAIM, EXECUTED WET. Production's own route over a declared output that was never
// written refuses, and the refusal carries git's REAL exit code and stderr as captured in this run
// -- the same command, the same workdir, the same absolute path, taken outside the capture step.
// The row also demands git itself refused (non-empty stderr, non-zero exit), so the comparison
// cannot be vacuous: if git ever reads a file nobody wrote, the row fails rather than passing on an
// empty expectation.
test fn the_wet_route_refuses_an_absent_output_with_gits_own_exit_and_stderr() -> Bool {
  let c = wet_capture_case(write_output: false, second_output_present: true)
  c.setup_failure == ""
    && c.contained
    && c.root_lists_own_writes
    && c.staging_as_expected
    && c.truth_stderr != ""
    && c.truth_exit != "0"
    && c.truth_exit != "<ok>"
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: "could not be hashed")
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: "git hash-object exited")
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: capture_rel_absent)
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: c.truth_exit)
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: c.truth_stderr)
}

// (3) THE EFFECT STOP, EXECUTED WET. With the FIRST of two declared outputs absent and the SECOND
// really on disk, production's route refuses at the first and runs no further effect: the staging
// tree stays empty -- the second output's install never happened -- and the refusal names the
// absent output and never the blob of the present one.
test fn the_wet_route_stops_at_the_first_absent_output_and_stages_nothing_after_it() -> Bool {
  let c = wet_capture_case(write_output: false, second_output_present: true)
  c.setup_failure == ""
    && c.contained
    && c.root_lists_own_writes
    && c.staging_as_expected
    && string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: capture_rel_absent)
    && !string_contains(s: c.verdict_text, pattern: capture_bytes_oid)
}
